{"sourceSha256": "df792ad977ad455a51986c63f475d6ddae4bc87734e6998c721188727ed94997", "text": "Dear Dr Wright,\nRe: Sandra Marcus, DOB: 15/01/83\n\nThank you for seeing Ms Marcus, a 36-year-old woman who requires assessment of an\nanterior swelling on her néck due to concerns of malignancy.\n\nMs Marcus initially presented on 05/07/19, with a 2-month history of a painless neck\n\nswelling. On examination, | observed a painless, anterior neck swelling, 2x2 cm in size,\nwhich moved with deglutition. There were no palpable lymph nodes, and CVS, RS and ABD\nexaminations were normal. | ordered thyroid function tests (TFTs) and an ultrasound of her\nneck.\n\nOn review two weeks later Ms Marcus reported no change. The TFT results were normal,\nbut the ultrasound showed multiple nodules with bilateral calcifications. | informed Ms\n\nMarcus of my provisional diagnosis, multi-nodular goitre, and advised a surgical review to\nrule out the possibility of malignancy. However, she was reluctant and defaulted her next\n\nappointment.\n\nToday, she presented with increased swelling, hoarseness of voice and difficulty in\n\nswallowing. The thyroid is firm with limited mobility, and there are some palpable lymph\n\nPlease note, Ms Marcus suffers from asthma, for which she uses a ventolin inhaler. She has\nno known allergies and is a single mother of 7-year-old child.\n\nIn view of the above, | would appreciate your urgent attention to her condition.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr Wright,\nRe: Sandra Marcus, DOB: 15/01/83\n\nThank you for seeing Ms Marcus, a 36-year-old woman who requires assessment of an\nanterior swelling on her néck due to concerns of malignancy.\n\nMs Marcus initially presented on 05/07/19, with a 2-month history of a painless neck\n\nswelling. On examination, | observed a painless, anterior neck swelling, 2x2 cm in size,\nwhich moved with deglutition. There were no palpable lymph nodes, and CVS, RS and ABD\nexaminations were normal. | ordered thyroid function tests (TFTs) and an ultrasound of her\nneck.\n\nOn review two weeks later Ms Marcus reported no change. The TFT results were normal,\nbut the ultrasound showed multiple nodules with bilateral calcifications. | informed Ms\n\nMarcus of my provisional diagnosis, multi-nodular goitre, and advised a surgical review to\nrule out the possibility of malignancy. However, she was reluctant and defaulted her next\n\nappointment.\n\nToday, she presented with increased swelling, hoarseness of voice and difficulty in\n\nswallowing. The thyroid is firm with limited mobility, and there are some palpable lymph\n\nPlease note, Ms Marcus suffers from asthma, for which she uses a ventolin inhaler. She has\nno known allergies and is a single mother of 7-year-old child.\n\nIn view of the above, | would appreciate your urgent attention to her condition.\n\nYours sincerely,\nDoctor", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2220.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr Wright,\nRe: Sandra Marcus, DOB: 15/01/83", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr Wright,", "x": 0.00901, "y": 0.01143, "width": 0.16396, "height": 0.01786, "confidence": 0.956, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.00901, "width": 0.05, "confidence": 0.96}, {"text": "Dr", "x": 0.06577, "width": 0.02523, "confidence": 0.95}, {"text": "Wright,", "x": 0.09595, "width": 0.07703, "confidence": 0.959}], "uncertainWords": []}, {"text": "Re: Sandra Marcus, DOB: 15/01/83", "x": 0.00946, "y": 0.0525, "width": 0.37072, "height": 0.01786, "confidence": 0.955, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.00946, "width": 0.03198, "confidence": 0.954}, {"text": "Sandra", "x": 0.04955, "width": 0.07387, "confidence": 0.954}, {"text": "Marcus,", "x": 0.13018, "width": 0.08153, "confidence": 0.963}, {"text": "DOB:", "x": 0.22072, "width": 0.05045, "confidence": 0.966}, {"text": "15/01/83", "x": 0.28108, "width": 0.0991, "confidence": 0.94}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Thank you for seeing Ms Marcus,